  "_comment": "D-1939: what an executor does with a cloud command whose signature verified, given the envelope it carries. services/api/src/__tests__/envelope-replay.test.ts holds the cloud's rules (envelopeFailures, envelopeVerdict) to these cases, and the Home Assistant add-on vendors this file (scripts/sync-edge-command-fixtures.sh) and holds its envelope_check.py to the same answers. The target inverter is payload.inverterId, as on the add-on; an empty one skips the inverter check. `now` is the executor's clock and `clockSet` whether it is trustworthy. `failed` lists the binding and validity checks that did not hold, in the board's fixed order (envelope_check.c). `verdict` gives the action at each enforcement level: `off` (the server's envelopeEnforce is false), `switch` (it is true) and `always` (the S3's always-enforce build). `run` runs the command, `refuse` acks it rejected with `reason`, and `retry_later` neither runs nor acks it. A planner_delegation (D-1714, removed 2026-11-21) fails planner_delegation alone and is refused with `command_mismatch` at every level, `off` included.",
